==Trivia==
*Love and Death's name is a reference to ''[[wikipedia:ja:愛と死|Ai to Shi]]'' ("''Love and Death''"), a novel published by [[wikipedia:Saneatsu Mushanokōji|Saneatsu Mushanokōji]] in 1939. The novel follows the character of Muraoka and his relationship with his friend's sister Natsuko, which they advance by writing to each other. They marry right before Muraoka sets off on a 6-month trip to Paris. The two continue to stay in contact via letters and have high hopes for their life as a married couple after Muraoka returns home, but on the ship back to Japan, Muraoka is informed that his wife had suddenly died of Spanish flu. After visiting her grave, Muraoka remarks that "the dead hold great power over the living, but the living are powerless over the dead."
*For [[April Fools' Jokes|April Fools' Day]] 2016, [[Let's Start Over]] was temporarily replaced by a version of Love and Death with lower strength magnifications.

